WEBVTT

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:15.640
My right hand holds a bowl of gold,

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:20.180
And my left holds one of silver.

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:24.720
Never one without the other,

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:37.800
Two unseen bowls for each of us.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:46.210
The golden one is filled with joy,

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:53.550
shining warmly.

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:58.350
Since we met, my golden bowl

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:05.360
cannot hold all my happiness and love.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:15.500
Golden joy, silver sadness,

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:22.850
I would leave my past behind...

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:27.580
For you, for the sake of love,

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:34.520
I would empty the bowls of my past.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:53.910
Give it to me please!

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:56.780
What are you going to do with it?

00:01:56.850 --> 00:02:00.180
I'll smoke it. I can smoke too!

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:02.450
No way.

00:02:02.650 --> 00:02:03.590
Yes I can!

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:05.720
Inhale then!

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:18.000
See? Now you understand.

00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:22.200
Don't smoke. It doesn't suit you.

00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:26.740
I want you staying just as you are... until the end of time.

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:30.750
I... I love you!

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:34.750
I love you!

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:41.290
<b>19. The Utakata Game</b>

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:50.700
Let's go back.

00:02:53.170 --> 00:02:56.640
If we hurry we can make the afternoon classes.

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:04.380
I... I love you!

00:03:13.190 --> 00:03:15.520
That was some surprise.

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:16.590
Huh?

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:19.600
...Rei having that girl with her...

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:24.600
I suppose it could happen, since both of them are Seiran students...

00:03:25.670 --> 00:03:29.810
...I bet both of them had morning classes, though.

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:34.880
We skipped classes in high school too, didn't we?

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:37.350
I guess so, but still...

00:03:43.490 --> 00:03:45.150
It's been a while, hasn't it? <b> </b>

00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:46.020
It's been a while, hasn't it? Huh?

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:48.020
Since the last time you saw Rei. <b> </b>

00:03:48.020 --> 00:03:49.090
Since the last time you saw Rei. Yes...

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:52.290
...and the last time you saw Orihara Kaoru.

00:03:54.630 --> 00:03:55.700
Yes...

00:03:59.370 --> 00:04:01.040
Are you really OK with that?

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:08.310
I have no choice.

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:10.650
I have no choice.

00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:26.200
I'll go on ahead!

00:04:32.670 --> 00:04:34.740
Dreamtime ends now.

00:04:49.480 --> 00:04:50.490
Nanako-san! <b> </b>

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:51.820
Nanako-san! Nanako!

00:04:51.820 --> 00:04:53.360
Um... Good morning.

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:57.560
Hey now! It's too late in the day for a "good morning"!

00:04:57.690 --> 00:04:59.830
What is it? Did something happen?

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:02.760
We called your house over and over!

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:04.100
You called my house??

00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:05.770
Nobody answered.

00:05:05.900 --> 00:05:08.700
Oh yes, Mom said she'd be out today...

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:11.510
What could possibly have happened to you today?

00:05:11.570 --> 00:05:14.640
Well, I... uh...

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:16.510
On the way to school I started feeling ill.

00:05:16.510 --> 00:05:19.920
...so I took a long rest at the coffee shop near the station.

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:23.050
So... how do you feel, now?

00:05:23.250 --> 00:05:26.720
I'm fine now. Sorry to make you worry.

00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:37.930
So at last, I finally said it.

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:41.940
I love you!

00:05:42.870 --> 00:05:44.010
It's done.

00:05:46.010 --> 00:05:48.340
That dreamlike moment,

00:05:48.340 --> 00:05:54.020
...that one moment alone with her... it is gone now.

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:57.840
I went to afternoon classes... then they were over...

00:05:58.820 --> 00:06:02.160
I thought I would become myself again.

00:06:03.430 --> 00:06:04.630
But I didn't.

00:06:05.290 --> 00:06:07.560
The dreamtime isn't over.

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:11.370
Instead, it is expanding, inflating like a giant bubble...

00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:14.770
...getting bigger and bigger.

00:06:18.510 --> 00:06:21.710
This morning Saint-Juste-sama was just sitting there...

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:31.650
Nanako! Nanako, for goodness sake!

00:06:31.720 --> 00:06:35.320
It's the last stop! The last stop! We're at the station!

00:06:44.730 --> 00:06:47.870
These familiar stores, and even the city itself,

00:06:47.870 --> 00:06:50.270
...have somehow taken on a new look today.

00:06:52.470 --> 00:06:56.080
You spent your 3000 Yen on THAT? What's with you??

00:06:56.080 --> 00:06:58.150
But it's so pretty!

00:07:00.150 --> 00:07:01.550
My dear Brother,

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:07.420
I think I want to cherish and care for my special "bubble"...

00:07:07.420 --> 00:07:09.220
...my big, inflated bubble...

00:07:09.220 --> 00:07:12.230
...and hope it doesn't burst!

00:07:13.100 --> 00:07:16.900
So, where is it? That cafe where you rested this morning?

00:07:16.900 --> 00:07:17.770
What?

00:07:18.030 --> 00:07:22.240
You know! The one you were at while you felt sick this morning.

00:07:22.300 --> 00:07:24.170
Oh! Oh! Um...

00:07:24.170 --> 00:07:26.780
You've seen it I'm sure... "Cafe la Moulin".

00:07:26.910 --> 00:07:29.310
Oh, Cafe la Moulin...? That one?

00:07:29.580 --> 00:07:33.050
Let's try one more... It looks so pretty on you!

00:07:33.250 --> 00:07:34.320
Really?

00:07:37.520 --> 00:07:41.590
But you know... Cafe la Moulin doesn't open until afternoon...

00:07:41.590 --> 00:07:42.320
What?

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:48.730
Well, let's go home...

00:07:49.060 --> 00:07:50.130
Tomoko...

00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:55.940
See you later. See you tomorrow.

00:07:56.470 --> 00:07:57.540
Tomoko!

00:07:57.740 --> 00:07:59.610
It's OK, it's all right!

00:07:59.610 --> 00:08:03.550
Today your face says "I'm happy!" and I really like it that way!

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:05.210
Tomoko!

00:08:06.150 --> 00:08:07.220
Tomoko...

00:08:08.820 --> 00:08:09.820
Tomoko.

00:08:09.890 --> 00:08:11.020
It's OK.

00:08:11.350 --> 00:08:14.090
Can you stay a little longer with me?

00:08:14.420 --> 00:08:15.420
I...

00:08:16.630 --> 00:08:18.630
I don't want to be alone.

00:08:18.630 --> 00:08:21.100
Suddenly I don't want to be alone...

00:09:09.010 --> 00:09:12.080
How is Rei doing in school?

00:09:14.420 --> 00:09:16.020
Why do you ask?

00:09:16.350 --> 00:09:18.420
Is she attending classes? Everyday?

00:09:18.550 --> 00:09:22.020
I don't know... I don't see much of her,

00:09:22.020 --> 00:09:24.290
...because she and I are in different grades.

00:09:24.560 --> 00:09:26.230
I saw her today.

00:09:26.230 --> 00:09:29.160
...in the park, in the morning, during classes.

00:09:32.370 --> 00:09:36.840
You're always acting as if you couldn't care less about her, but...

00:09:39.980 --> 00:09:42.180
Rei "kidnapped" a freshman today.

00:09:42.510 --> 00:09:44.450
Do you know Misonoo Nanako?

00:09:45.780 --> 00:09:47.520
Yes, barely...

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:50.590
We inducted her into the sorority this year.

00:09:50.850 --> 00:09:53.060
Is she close to Rei?

00:09:53.720 --> 00:09:54.790
I don't know.

00:09:56.990 --> 00:10:00.260
I hope Rei doesn't corrupt her...

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:08.140
I should be going.

00:10:10.940 --> 00:10:14.880
Brother, how did you become acquainted with this freshman?

00:10:16.680 --> 00:10:18.680
Well, never mind...

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:19.750
Good night.

00:10:20.820 --> 00:10:21.750
Good night.

00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:46.310
I didn't want to be alone.

00:10:47.640 --> 00:10:50.050
I didn't want to be alone, today.

00:10:53.850 --> 00:10:56.590
I... I love you!

00:10:58.520 --> 00:11:01.260
That's the first time I've ever said those words.

00:11:01.790 --> 00:11:05.460
I've heard myself thinking those words,

00:11:05.460 --> 00:11:11.200
...but I never thought I would say them.

00:11:11.200 --> 00:11:15.670
...not aloud, not face-to-face, I thought.

00:11:16.870 --> 00:11:19.680
That's why I couldn't bear being alone.

00:11:20.940 --> 00:11:22.280
I'm back...

00:11:22.280 --> 00:11:23.410
Welcome home.

00:11:23.550 --> 00:11:25.010
You're late today, Nanako.

00:11:25.210 --> 00:11:28.880
Before you go upstairs... would you come to the living room?

00:11:28.880 --> 00:11:30.350
Yes, only one moment... <b> </b>

00:11:30.350 --> 00:11:31.090
Yes, only one moment... What?

00:11:31.150 --> 00:11:34.360
Your father's done it again...!

00:11:34.360 --> 00:11:36.230
Yes, I guess I did...

00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:40.560
I wondered if it was a bit too young...

00:11:40.630 --> 00:11:44.170
It was in a display window at a store near the university.

00:11:44.170 --> 00:11:48.240
I was sure it would look good on you, so I bought it.

00:11:50.440 --> 00:11:51.770
Thank you, Daddy!

00:11:51.910 --> 00:11:54.910
It might make a good party dress.

00:12:03.320 --> 00:12:05.050
Thank you, Daddy...

00:12:25.410 --> 00:12:29.080
Ma cherie La Poupee... She looks just like you.

00:12:34.680 --> 00:12:37.150
I knew what would be in store for me,

00:12:37.150 --> 00:12:39.220
...when I finally was able to be alone.

00:12:44.360 --> 00:12:46.300
See, now it's starting.

00:12:49.830 --> 00:12:52.100
Oh... Saint-Juste-sama!

00:12:52.770 --> 00:12:55.100
I told Saint-Juste-sama!

00:12:55.100 --> 00:12:57.370
How was I able to speak to her like that?

00:12:57.370 --> 00:13:00.180
How on earth does she feel about me now?

00:13:04.110 --> 00:13:05.650
Saint-Juste-sama! <b> </b>

00:13:05.650 --> 00:13:06.050
Saint-Juste-sama! Saint-Juste-sama!

00:13:06.050 --> 00:13:07.180
Saint-Juste-sama!

00:13:23.470 --> 00:13:25.670
Hey, keep it down in the gallery!!

00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:30.070
This isn't a regular season game. It's just a scrimmage!

00:13:30.670 --> 00:13:33.010
You're all welcome to watch quietly.

00:13:33.010 --> 00:13:35.280
...but we can do without all the screaming!

00:13:35.410 --> 00:13:37.950
How about a picture of you and Saint-Juste-sama together?

00:13:37.950 --> 00:13:40.080
...maybe later after the game, please?

00:14:01.100 --> 00:14:02.570
Well I don't know about all this.

00:14:03.570 --> 00:14:08.180
I've been trying to get you to practice with us,

00:14:08.180 --> 00:14:11.110
...but can't you do something about your "groupies"?

00:14:11.310 --> 00:14:13.180
Maybe we should spray them with insecticide...?

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:22.190
You've gotten really cocky!

00:14:22.190 --> 00:14:24.190
No, it just doesn't mean much to me.

00:14:24.530 --> 00:14:28.330
Anyway, I'm counting on you to start the next game.

00:14:29.260 --> 00:14:32.400
Does this mean the end of Seiran basketball, I wonder?

00:14:49.080 --> 00:14:51.750
Was it foolish to speak up like that to her?

00:14:51.750 --> 00:14:54.560
I can't even say "hello" like I used to, anymore...

00:14:54.560 --> 00:14:57.960
And while I'm thinking all this, what is she thinking?

00:15:02.430 --> 00:15:05.170
Is she one of your groupies, too?

00:15:05.230 --> 00:15:06.100
What?

00:15:06.240 --> 00:15:10.110
That one... watching you from behind the tree.

00:15:10.840 --> 00:15:11.910
What are you talking about?

00:15:13.180 --> 00:15:14.240
OK, nevermind then...

00:15:18.650 --> 00:15:22.180
She's an acquaintance of Henmi Takehiko.

00:15:34.800 --> 00:15:36.800
Yesterday, at the park.

00:15:36.800 --> 00:15:40.670
We ran into him and my brother there.

00:15:41.870 --> 00:15:45.340
Henmi was still the same old Henmi Takehiko.

00:15:51.080 --> 00:15:53.350
I've forgotten him. Completely.

00:16:02.620 --> 00:16:07.030
We were able to translate literally up to here.

00:16:07.230 --> 00:16:10.230
The important part begins at line 18.

00:16:10.770 --> 00:16:13.300
So... let's see... Miss Misonoo...?

00:16:13.840 --> 00:16:16.100
Oh! Nanako! Your turn!

00:16:16.370 --> 00:16:17.710
Uh, yes!

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:20.840
Would you translate from line 18, please?

00:16:20.980 --> 00:16:21.980
OK!

00:16:22.710 --> 00:16:24.580
Not the literal meaning, please.

00:16:24.580 --> 00:16:28.580
Express the text using your own feeling for the meanings within it.

00:16:28.580 --> 00:16:29.790
Go for it!

00:16:31.650 --> 00:16:33.120
Go right ahead, please.

00:16:33.260 --> 00:16:34.260
OK!

00:16:35.660 --> 00:16:37.790
<i>Ai no Hyohaku-sha...</i> Wanderer of Love...

00:16:37.930 --> 00:16:39.330
<i>"Koi no"</i>

00:16:39.530 --> 00:16:43.530
Because of the context, <i>"Koi"</i> would be better here.

00:16:43.670 --> 00:16:47.740
And try <i>"sasuraibito"</i> instead of <i>"hyohaku-sha"</i> for "wanderer".

00:16:48.140 --> 00:16:49.270
O... OK.

00:16:49.940 --> 00:16:55.940
A wanderer of love, I hear the whistle through the evening glow.

00:16:57.080 --> 00:16:58.350
Yes, very good!

00:16:58.810 --> 00:17:04.690
The last train leaving the city has just departed.

00:17:05.750 --> 00:17:10.830
Once again, I am not on that train. Once again, I am not leaving.

00:17:11.910 --> 00:17:18.470
Once again, I can't bear to face the depth of my own heartbreak.

00:17:19.430 --> 00:17:21.170
Dusk is approaching.

00:17:25.590 --> 00:17:30.550
Dusk is approaching. Once again, I wait, dreading the coming solitude.

00:17:31.650 --> 00:17:37.010
I sit alone on these tracks, tracks reddened with rust.

00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:42.340
Far in the distance... do I hear another whistle...?

00:17:44.770 --> 00:17:49.060
Did I hear it? Or just imagine it...

00:17:51.430 --> 00:17:52.430
Nanako-san! <b> </b>

00:17:52.430 --> 00:17:52.900
Nanako-san! What's wrong? Easy, easy!

00:17:52.900 --> 00:17:55.180
What's wrong? Easy, easy!

00:18:08.680 --> 00:18:10.290
I'd like a window seat, please.

00:18:10.420 --> 00:18:11.630
Yes, ma'am.

00:18:12.580 --> 00:18:13.520
Have a seat.

00:18:13.650 --> 00:18:14.460
OK.

00:18:15.350 --> 00:18:18.900
We're close to the ocean, so there are lots of seagulls flying about.

00:18:20.390 --> 00:18:21.390
Do you like seagulls?

00:18:21.530 --> 00:18:23.270
What? Yes.

00:18:23.960 --> 00:18:25.030
Have you heard?

00:18:25.310 --> 00:18:27.590
The Seiran cafeteria's fried chicken...

00:18:27.590 --> 00:18:30.210
...is actually fried seagull?

00:18:30.210 --> 00:18:31.010
What!?

00:18:32.830 --> 00:18:34.780
It's in the hamburgers, too.

00:18:34.780 --> 00:18:35.780
What?!!

00:18:54.290 --> 00:18:57.780
Anything I say that doesn't make you laugh, seems to make you cry instead....

00:18:57.940 --> 00:19:00.150
I'm sorry, I'm sorry....

00:19:00.150 --> 00:19:02.570
I'm strange. I'm not myself lately.

00:19:02.570 --> 00:19:04.170
It isn't all that strange.

00:19:04.710 --> 00:19:08.930
Falling in love makes all of us feel a bit strange, you know.

00:19:10.890 --> 00:19:13.640
I wanted to tell you something. So I invited you here.

00:19:14.290 --> 00:19:18.450
If it is Rei you've fallen in love with, you're going to be hurt...

00:19:20.390 --> 00:19:25.350
Because Rei's soul is enslaved to a goddess.

00:19:28.630 --> 00:19:29.970
That's all I had to say.

00:19:33.340 --> 00:19:38.500
They say "to love is to suffer"...

00:19:39.130 --> 00:19:41.810
I suppose that's all right if you're the only one hurt by it.

00:19:42.290 --> 00:19:46.240
Of course, one avoids hurting the other, if possible...

00:19:46.870 --> 00:19:49.810
If that's love, then I'd like to fall in love, too...

00:19:55.510 --> 00:19:57.250
I can forget, because I love.

00:19:57.960 --> 00:19:59.770
I can forget, because I've loved.

00:20:00.200 --> 00:20:04.890
And even... I'll even forget that I've forgotten.

00:20:06.130 --> 00:20:07.610
I loved you that much...

00:20:14.680 --> 00:20:17.090
I almost asked "Did YOU hurt the one you love?"

00:20:18.640 --> 00:20:23.330
...but then I saw that she had loved so very deeply,

00:20:25.540 --> 00:20:29.360
...her love was so profound,

00:20:29.360 --> 00:20:36.400
...that it was beyond my ability to even imagine,

00:20:36.400 --> 00:20:41.350
...and that even now she might still feel that way.

00:20:47.030 --> 00:20:50.110
Love is <i>"utakata".  "Utakata" no koi.</i>

00:20:50.480 --> 00:20:51.420
<i>UTAKATA?</i>

00:20:51.930 --> 00:20:53.870
Yes, <i>utakata.</i>

00:20:53.870 --> 00:20:56.210
Love is just like a bubble...

00:20:56.210 --> 00:21:00.430
It pops to the surface, lingers for an instant, and is soon gone.

00:21:01.820 --> 00:21:05.240
Life's fleeting instant is like a bubble too.

00:21:05.240 --> 00:21:12.070
So, all of us in that brief bubble seek to love and be loved...

00:21:12.070 --> 00:21:14.210
Its beauty lies in its brevity.

00:21:17.220 --> 00:21:21.570
But we must never despise it for being merely ephemeral.

00:21:21.860 --> 00:21:23.400
Wouldn't you agree?

00:21:25.460 --> 00:21:28.470
That's how we should look at it.

00:21:29.650 --> 00:21:31.390
Yes!

00:21:45.400 --> 00:21:46.340
Yes...?

00:21:46.490 --> 00:21:49.910
I've been thinking about... the old days.

00:21:51.750 --> 00:21:54.090
The day I first met you.

00:21:55.350 --> 00:21:56.830
I... uh...

00:21:56.890 --> 00:22:00.710
You were 10, and I was 11...

00:22:01.760 --> 00:22:05.840
It was in our back yard. Do you remember?

00:22:06.610 --> 00:22:09.350
Uh... yes, of course!

00:22:09.690 --> 00:22:12.170
I was crying.

00:22:20.760 --> 00:22:22.230
You were the only one...

00:22:22.830 --> 00:22:23.770
Yes!

00:22:24.120 --> 00:22:25.930
...the only one to see me cry.

00:22:26.470 --> 00:22:27.340
Yes!

00:22:27.760 --> 00:22:30.040
You were the only one, my sister...

00:22:30.930 --> 00:22:31.930
Yes!

00:22:32.520 --> 00:22:37.010
That's why you must look only at ME.

00:22:37.800 --> 00:22:41.620
Understand? You must never look at anyone else.

00:23:25.440 --> 00:23:26.980
My dear brother...

00:23:27.300 --> 00:23:30.520
Should I have kept these words to myself?

00:23:30.870 --> 00:23:33.620
Should this have remained my secret forever?

00:23:34.090 --> 00:23:38.720
But... but I... was helpless to hold it in!

00:23:42.510 --> 00:23:45.800
I love you, Saint-Juste-sama!

00:24:10.160 --> 00:24:14.360
I dreamed I was chasing a rainbow...

00:24:14.360 --> 00:24:19.830
Then the rainbow I was chasing was you.

00:24:21.300 --> 00:24:25.440
Before, I had no strength, no will.

00:24:25.440 --> 00:24:30.910
But now because of you, I do.

00:24:31.650 --> 00:24:37.190
Feelings of love, like raindrops

00:24:37.190 --> 00:24:42.660
Come pouring from the sky.

00:24:42.660 --> 00:24:45.390
This is surely a game

00:24:45.390 --> 00:24:48.200
Of some mischievous fairy...

00:24:48.200 --> 00:24:50.600
Always dancing,

00:24:50.600 --> 00:24:55.870
Always capricious...

00:25:01.460 --> 00:25:04.070
Preview

00:25:04.070 --> 00:25:06.150
Henmi invites Nanako to attend a university fair,

00:25:06.150 --> 00:25:07.620
...and Nanako is thrilled to accept.

00:25:07.820 --> 00:25:12.180
But, Fukiko becomes upset upon hearing of it.

00:25:12.710 --> 00:25:14.580
On the day of the university fair,

00:25:14.580 --> 00:25:18.670
...Fukiko calls Nanako to the sorority house.

00:25:18.930 --> 00:25:20.010
And then...

00:25:20.960 --> 00:25:21.900
Next episode: <b> </b>

00:25:21.900 --> 00:25:23.370
Next episode: <b>The Gardening Shears</b>

00:25:23.570 --> 00:25:25.110
Brother, Dear Brother... <b> </b>

00:25:25.110 --> 00:25:28.530
Brother, Dear Brother... There is no end to my tears...
